    "prompt_mask": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nB=@@M0@@,\\,C=@@M1@@,\\,D=@@M2@@.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $BC=CB={I}_{2}$\n- **II.** $BD=DB={I}_{2}$\n- **III.** $D={B}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
    "solution_mask": "- First, we check whether $BC=CB={I}_{2}.$ Computing $BC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =@@M0@@@@M1@@ \\\\  & =@@P0@@ \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false.\n\n- Now, we check whether $BD=DB={I}_{2}.$ Computing $BD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BD & =@@M0@@@@M2@@ \\\\  & =@@P1@@ \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DB & =@@M2@@@@M0@@ \\\\  & =@@P2@@ \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. As a result, $D={B}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
